WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:05.520
"Star Wars" fans rejoice: the Witches&nbsp;
of Dathomir have made their long-awaited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.080
live-action debut! First introduced in&nbsp;
the now-Legends novel "The Courtship of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.040
Princess Leia," the witches eventually saw&nbsp;
their entrance into canon territory when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:17.940
they appeared in Dave Filoni's "Star Wars:&nbsp;
The Clone Wars." In the animated series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.880
the Daughters of Dathomir,&nbsp;
also called the Nightsisters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:26.400
amazed and baffled audiences by bathing in dark&nbsp;
side energy and wielding ancient magick powers;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.140
the witches certainly weren't Jedi, but they&nbsp;
didn't fully align with Sith beliefs either.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:36.180
Now, the witches and their crimson robes have&nbsp;
returned, in league with Grand Admiral Thrawn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:40.860
no less. In the latest episode of "Ahsoka,"&nbsp;
the magick wielders are waiting on Peridea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.060
for Morgan Elsbeth to arrive with her&nbsp;
retinue. There are three witches, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:49.380
"Star Wars" fans may want to know who the actors&nbsp;
are bringing these mysterious characters to life.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:55.020
Bringing to life the Great Mother Aktropaw&nbsp;
is none other than Jeryl Prescott. Without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.820
her scarlet robes and eerie makeup, longtime&nbsp;
"Walking Dead" fans probably recognize this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:04.860
actor. Prescott was one of the core characters&nbsp;
in the show's first season. She portrayed Jacqui,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:09.900
one of the first characters who stood up to&nbsp;
Carol's abusive husband, Ed. Jacqui perished at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.640
the end of the season when she decided to remain&nbsp;
behind at the CDC, which was timed to explode.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:19.560
In recent years, Prescott has taken prominent&nbsp;
recurring roles in shows like "All the Queen's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:25.020
Men" and "Swamp Thing." The latter wasn't her&nbsp;
only DC project as she also was in an episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:30.540
of "Batwoman." Prior to that, she played in&nbsp;
episodes of "Shameless," "Scandal," and "NCIS: Los&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:37.020
Angeles." In 2014, she also guest-starred in five&nbsp;
episodes on Showtime's hit series, "Ray Donovan."

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:40.800
While "Ahsoka" may be the actor's&nbsp;
first time in a galaxy far, far away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.280
she is obviously no Padawan&nbsp;
when it comes to performing!

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:51.000
Jane Edwina Seymour portrays Lakesis, the&nbsp;
Dathomirian witch who informs Morgan Elsbeth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.860
of Thrawn's incoming arrival. The actor was&nbsp;
very thrilled to join the "Star Wars" universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.860 --> 00:02:01.020
having frequently expressed her excitement on her&nbsp;
social media before "Ahsoka" debuted, writing,

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:04.020
"Excited for this to go to air...and very grateful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:08.400
to be a part of this STAR WARS series,&nbsp;
I loved working on it in so many ways."

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:13.260
Seymour is no stranger to the world of&nbsp;
sci-fi, having recently appeared in two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:16.560
episodes of "Star Trek: Picard"&nbsp;
as the Borg Queen. Before that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:20.940
Seymour took part in more grounded dramas&nbsp;
such as "Nova Vita," playing Dr. Perkins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.420
and starring alongside names like&nbsp;
Titus Welliver and Dean Norris.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:28.020
Eagle-eyed fans of Netflix's&nbsp;
"You" may also recognize her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:32.940
as she played a hilariously upbeat and sort&nbsp;
of inappropriate library goer who compliments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:37.680
Joe Goldberg's child just a bit too much.&nbsp;
Thankfully, she only appeared in a single&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:42.480
episode in the show's third season, any longer&nbsp;
and she may have had to endure Joe's wrath.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:46.440
Portraying Klothow, who appears&nbsp;
to be the leading Great Mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:52.140
is video game legend Claudia Black. Longtime&nbsp;
gamers may have recognized Klothow's voice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:55.440
as the actor has been a part&nbsp;
of several iconic franchises.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:00.660
Interestingly, Black's most famous voice role is&nbsp;
arguably that of Morrigan from Bioware's "Dragon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:06.000
Age" series; Morrigan is a Witch of the Wilds&nbsp;
and one of the main companions in "Dragon Age:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:11.160
Origins." Talk about perfect casting! The actor&nbsp;
also has roles in two "Mass Effect" games,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:16.560
another signature Bioware franchise. Black&nbsp;
has also voiced roles for popular titles like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.000
"Call of Duty," "Uncharted," and "Gears of&nbsp;
War." And that barely scratches the surface.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:25.320
On top of her several gaming roles, Black&nbsp;
recently guest-starred in four episodes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:31.140
of HBO's "The Nevers." In 2022, she leapt&nbsp;
into another live-action sci-fi project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:34.320
taking on the leading role&nbsp;
of Karla Grey in "Deus."

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:37.860
Aside from voicing countless&nbsp;
iconic video game characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:42.120
Black is probably best known for her&nbsp;
early recurring roles on "Farscape"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:47.880
and "Stargate SG-1," shows that are considered&nbsp;
absolute gems and staples in the sci-fi genre.

